**Goal**: move iss_build==0 *config* OIDs off the in-master ies-auto-mibs REST loopback onto the app_moxa_framework AgentX subagent (in-process `config_operation::get_config_from_path` GET ~4ms; SET stays REST PATCH via `ies_config_set*`). Measured win: REST 16.8ms vs AgentX 12.5ms → ~4.3ms/OID. The customer "50ms" is ifTable/ifXTable, already served natively by ISS — separate from this. Decided AGAINST the "move all ies-auto-mibs into framework" pivot (Option A spike: `init_ies_auto_mibs` has snmpd-coupled side-effects — rm/mkdir /moxa/run/auto_mibs, s_token mgmt — and dual fetch LibFrameworkUri+iss_uri_read_inplace). Staying with per-group reuse.

**How it works** (`dl/lib_moxa_ies_auto_mibs/src/mapping_reuse.c`): `#include`s the canonical `net_*.h` arrays + product -D flags; `g_reuse_srcs[]` (REUSE_SRC macro) lists migrated groups; each group's `MOX_SNMP_INIT_ENTRY` is commented in `3rdparty_net_snmp/ies-auto-mibs/ies_auto_mibs_setup.c` (needs `make 3rdparty_net_snmp-dirclean`). Filters `iss_build != 0` (serve iss0 only). `ies_map_entry.table_col`: 0=scalar, 1=portsPbmp index (→port), 2=portsPbmp value (flat bool array[port-1], N from `LibSystem_GetMaxPortNumInSystem`), 3=index-table value (path `<uri><row-1>/<column>` via get_config_from_path, register 1..REUSE_MAX_TABLE_ROWS=16, noSuchInstance past array end), 4=index-table index (existence check → row). Index-table only for groups with setup==NULL (turboring has a setup fn → its tables stay special). Handler `app_moxa_framework/src/snmp_subagent.rs`. portsPbmp SET = whole-array read-modify-write (`ies_config_set_json`); index-table SET = path-addressable `config_set*`.

**Roadmap**: A = pure config-scalar groups (no new code). B = generic index-table handler (DONE) → unlocks trap/portmirror/trustAccess/ipIfdb/device_io/snmp. C = turboringv2 (needs status layer `rust_moxa_status_operation::get_status_from_path` + named-key ring table, biggest). mxDot1xdb = mixed group (3 iss0 localDatabase at `.603.4.5.2.2` + 16 iss1 at ISS `.5.1.x`; split works cleanly — disjoint OIDs, no priority games; needs iss_build filter [done] + B + password mask).

**Current state**: A migrated 8 groups (event_switching/general/poe/routing/tracking, email, loginPolicy, passwordPolicy, RMON) — VERIFIED on DUT. B index-table handler VERIFIED via **syslog** (`.8691.602.8.2`): GET (3 fixed rows, index+value cols, existence-checked) + path-addressable single-field SET both work. Also verified earlier: system_information, portEvent (+portsPbmp GET/SET), event_general, turboringv2 scalars, chainProtectEvent fix.
**C step 1 (status-layer read path) = DONE & VERIFIED.** Implemented `is_status` field (set when net_*.h `.uri` starts with `stat/`) → handler `handle_status_get` uses `status_operation.get_status_from_path(&mut plugins_status, path, &ui, &QString::from(""))`; status entries are RONLY (notWritable on SET). SubagentState now carries `status_operation` + `plugins_status` (passed from uri_service.rs:123); added `qstring="0.7.2"` dep. Verified on DUT: turboring `coupling/portStatus` `.603.3.4.2.2.1.0` returns a value (was noSuchInstance). Note: ringIndex/totalRingNumber/dynRingCoupTable `.603.3.4.3.x` are under `#if defined(MOXA_DRC)` and MOXA_DRC is OFF on MDS-G4012 (BR2_MOXA_DRC not set) → correctly absent (No Such Object), matches in-master — NOT a bug. The status read path is now reusable for device_io (DI/DO) and other stat/ groups.

**C step 2 (turboring config ring table) = DONE & VERIFIED.** Added `IES_COL_TR2RING_VALUE` (=5): path `<uri>/ring<row>/<column>` (1-based named key `ring1/ring2`, via ies-auto-mibs URI_MOD_BY_IDX `uHandle_turboringv2_config_ring_table` = `turboringv2/ring%d/%s`). `is_turboring_ring` (uri=="config/turboringv2/ring/", cols index/enable/master) expands TR2_RING_NUM=2 rows. Verified on DUT (no physical ring — config default has ring1/ring2 disabled): `.603.3.4.1.2.1.{1=index,2=enable,3=master}.{1,2}` all return values (index 1/2, enable/master both 2=false), master column NO drift, stop-framework confirms framework serves it. interface col (`.4.x`, REDUNDANT_PORT) deferred; ring STATUS table + dynRingCoup deferred (dynRingCoup is DRC-off anyway). **Also refactored table_col magic numbers → named consts: C `IES_COL_*` in lib_moxa_ies_auto_mibs.h (single source) + Rust `col::*` mirror in lib_moxa_rust_ies_auto_mibs; both mapping_reuse.c + snmp_subagent.rs use names.**

Remaining turboring (low ROI, disabled feature, 0 gap vs NOS7): interface REDUNDANT_PORT col + status ring table (`stat/turboringv2/ring/` masterStatus/brokenStatus — needs status path + ring<N> format). Recommend NEXT: use status path on **device_io** (cleaner payoff) or move on; turboring is essentially done for the config side.

Older C starting notes (still valid for reference):
- Add `status_operation: Arc<Mutex<rust_moxa_status_operation::StatusOperation>>` + `plugins_status: Arc<Mutex<plugins_moxa_framework::status::Plugins>>` to `SubagentState`; they exist in AppState, built in `app_moxa_framework/src/uri_service.rs` (~lines 93/111), pass into `start_snmp_subagent` (call at uri_service.rs:123).
- Status read: `status_operation.lock().get_status_from_path(&mut plugins_status, path, &ui, &QString::from(""))` (`rust_moxa_status_operation/src/lib.rs:281`). Needs `qstring` crate dep in app_moxa_framework/Cargo.toml (used via `qstring::QString`).
- Detect status entries: original net_*.h `.uri` starts with `stat/` (setup remaps stat/turboringv2/... → turboringv2/...); add an `is_status` flag to `ies_map_entry` (C + Rust MapEntry), set in mapping_reuse when `strncmp(e->uri,"stat/",5)==0`; handler branches to status layer when set. This unlocks the 3 turboring status scalars (ringIndex/totalRingNumber/coupling portStatus) first (contained, testable).
- turboring TABLES (config ring + status ring + dynRingCoup) are named-key (`{ring1:{...},ring2:{...}}`) via URI_MOD_BY_IDX (`handle_uri_mod_by_idx_table` builds `IES_URI_CONFIG_PATH("/%s%d/%s")` = uri+idx+col) — bigger, do after the status scalars work.
Then: mxDot1xdb, then hard B tables (RowStatus/nested/named-scalar).

**B remaining groups are NOT a clean batch** (vetted): the generic index-table handler only fits SIMPLE tables like syslog (fixed-size array, flat columns, no RowStatus). Each other config-table group has a complication:
- `mx_device_io` (io/status.rs) = DI/DO STATUS not config → skip (like generalInfo).
- `mx_trap_notification`, `mx_trustAccess` = READ_CREATE/RowStatus tables; trustAccess+portmirror source is plugin `iss.rs` (maybe ISS-bridged, verify).
- `mxIpIfdb` (l3VlanIfTable) = RowStatus + nested columns (`ipv4.ipAddress` — the `<uri><row-1>/<column>` path may not resolve a dotted key) + dynamic-length (VLANs), not fixed maxItems.
- `mx_snmp` = has scalars with uri_index != "0" (engineID/engineBOOT… oid_index=0) that `is_scalar` (only matches uri_index=="0") SKIPS + userAccountTable (v3). 
Follow-ups needed for these: RowStatus support, nested/dotted column paths, named-uri_index scalars, and status-layer read (shared with C).

**GOTCHAS / lessons**:
- Only migrate groups whose data is truly in `running_config` (has a config plugin). **generalInfo was a bad pick** — device/system info (port#/MAC/serial/model/version), NOT config (no `generalInfo` config plugin), uses Counter32/MAC_ADDRESS types the handler doesn't do → reverted to in-master (still on REST). To move it needs bespoke `lib_moxa_rust_system` LibSystem calls + Counter32/MAC types in the agentx wrapper.
- chainProtectEvent-style name drift (net_*.h URI ≠ plugin config key) → fix at source (rename), not mod_uri. Walk each migrated group to catch drift (noSuchInstance).
- Product `#if` guards: skip groups not compiled (dhcpSrv/event_hardware/managementIP absent; event_routing needs INCLUDE_MOXA_L3, event_tracking needs MOXA_TRACKING — both present, wrapped in #if in mapping_reuse).
- SET (all iss0 + iss1) stays REST by design (rare + reuses full setting_write pipeline) — fine.
